    {
      "title": "Indian table tennis players bag five bronze medals at Asian Para Games 2026",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/sports/asian-games/indian-table-tennis-players-bag-five-bronze-medals-at-asian-para-games-2026-126102000218_1.html",
      "description": "Ravi Baby Sahana and Prachi Pandey scripted history by becoming India's first para table tennis players to make the podium in the standing category at the Asian Para Games, as the country secured five bronze medals here on Tuesday.\nParalympics medallist Bhavina Patel, Sonalben Patel, Prachi and Sahana all went down to accomplished Paralympic medallists in their respective women's singles semifinals, while Jehan Madan bagged a bronze medal in the men's singles class 1 event by virtue of finishing fourth in a five-paddler field.\nThe haul also took India past its medal tally from the previous edition, where it had won two bronze medals in para table tennis.\nSahana and Prachi's bronze were particularly significant as they became the first Indians to win medals in the standing category at the Asian Para Games.\nTamil Nadu's Sahana went down 8-11, 2-11, 4-11 to five-time Paralympic gold medallist Mao Jingdian of China in the Class 9 semifinal.\nClass 9 in para table tennis is a standing .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-20T08:08:53"
    }
